  "notes": "Biomechanics option, University Park (of four options — Biopharmaceutical, Medical Imaging, Medical Device Design are the others, each with its own distinct prescribed courses and elective-slot names/counts; would need separate degree-plan JSON files to model). Verified 2026-08-27 against the BME department's real, live elective-list page (https://www.bme.psu.edu/students/undergraduate/list-of-elective-courses-by-options.aspx), not just the bulletin -- confirmed 'Biomechanics Elective' is the verbatim real label, not a misnomer. Wired via 'match'/'open_elective' using the department's real course lists. Fixed 2 real discrepancies against the current bulletin: BME 409 (Biofluid Mechanics), a prescribed/required course for this option, was missing entirely -- added (Semester 6). EMCH 316 was misplaced one semester late (bulletin: paired with EMCH 315 in Semester 5, not Semester 6) -- moved. 'Related Technical Elective' real rule (any BME 400+, CHEM 210/212, ENGR 295/395/495, or approved-minor courses) is broader than a closed list -- wired as open_elective at 400+ (CHEM 210/212 not independently addable without conflicting with the mechanism, documented gap). 'Science or Engineering Elective' real rule (CHEM/PHYS/MATH/BIOL/STAT/BMB, or 'any College of Engineering course,' at 300+) -- wired to the CHEM/PHYS/MATH/BIOL/STAT/BMB subset only; the 'any Engineering college course' clause is far broader than this plan's department list and is a documented gap, not fabricated. Post-prereq-parser-fix repair (unrelated to the handbook review, left largely as-is): CHEM 110's real catalog prereq is MATH 22, which was never in this plan, so MATH 21/MATH 22 (Semester 2) were added as an engine-only fallback chain for a hypothetical student with no reported math placement (see expand_math_placement in planner_engine.py). Removed 2026-08-27: MATH 3 and MATH 4 (previously in Semester 1), added on the theory that MATH 21 needs MATH 4 needs MATH 3 -- math_catalog.json's own MATH 21 entry has an empty prereq_groups (no prerequisite at all), and MATH 3/MATH 4 are separately hardcoded as unconditionally satisfied everywhere by expand_math_placement regardless of any student input. They were dead weight inflating the plan by 6 phantom credits with zero effect on schedulability (verified via build_full_plan) -- removed.",
